{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"d42cff6908f845c9625fb51a0f01a7f711f21f5ed2d3976436ce485ff061cbaa","digest":{"component_or_area":"gate verdict plumbing and exit-code routing (plan-review, code-review, completion-verify)","key_entities":["gate_dispatch.py::_degraded_plan_review_verdict","gate_dispatch.py::_degraded_code_review_verdict","transition_close.py::_completion_precheck","transition_close.py::close_ticket","_llm_commands.py::_review_plan","_llm_commands.py::_review_code","_llm_commands.py::_verify_completion","code_review/shim.py::_verdict_to_review_result","_mcp_llm.py::review_plan","_mcp_llm.py::review_code","_mcp_llm.py::verify_completion","signing.py::sign_manifest","plan_review_verdict.schema.json","code_review_verdict.schema.json","completion_verdict.schema.json","docs/exit-codes.md","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py","LLMOutcome::resolution_class","LLMOutcome::retryable","CommandError::returncode","coverage.resolution_class","coverage.retryable","coverage.diagnostic"],"problem_keywords":["exit code 11","retryable failure","llm degradation","verdict plumbing","never-sign guard","systemic block","resolution class","diagnostic sanitization","gate wiring","fail-open preservation"],"propositions":["Retryable LLM failures (WAIT_AND_RETRY, RETRY_NOW) must exit 11 (block-but-retryable) across plan-review, code-review, and completion-verify gates, distinct from exit 2 (indeterminate) and existing passes/blocks.","The LLMOutcome object carrying resolution_class and retryable bool must flow through shape-A verdict dicts (plan/code-review) and shape-B exception paths (completion-precheck) so all downstream CLI consumers read the persisted or exception-attached disposition directly without re-deriving retryability.","Per-criterion fail-open must be preserved: a single flaky finder among N must not block a claim, and per-finder failure does not cascade to systemic block.","A degraded verdict (any non-PASS or non-null resolution_class) must structurally refuse signing via a guard at the sign-decision caller, ensuring the never-sign invariant is regression-testable and not buried in generic sign_manifest logic.","The pre-sign head-SHA fingerprint (verified-at-sha from the manifest) must be re-checked inside the write lock immediately before signing; on code drift, the close succeeds unsigned and exits 0 with a stderr warning, and verify remains outside the write lock.","Sanitized diagnostic and class-specific actionable message must be written to session log at both shape-A and shape-B degrade sites via append_session_log (best-effort, never fails the gate), and the message must be printed to stderr with the resolution_class for human troubleshooting."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785818891410544108,"uuid":"6fdfca47-bc90-4329-8cbe-b8991cc9357f"}